diff --git a/docs/acceptance/M1.5.md b/docs/acceptance/M1.5.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..5227e6b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/acceptance/M1.5.md
@@ -0,0 +1,56 @@
+# M1.5 — SQLite connection status and recoverable failures
+
+**Status:** Implementation patch prepared; local Windows/Linux validation pending.
+**Base:** M1.1 + M1.2 test fix + M1.3; M1.4 UI is not required by this patch.
+
+## Scope
+
+- Reject empty and non-SQLite files before `SQLITE_OPEN_READ_WRITE` can initialize them.
+- Return distinct structured errors for missing files, access denied, invalid header,
+  duplicate connection, connection not found, and connection limits.
+- Normalize to a single active connection for each canonical file path, regardless
+  of requested read-only/read-write mode. Duplicate opens return
+  `CONNECTION_ALREADY_OPEN`; the user must close and reopen to change mode.
+  **This intentionally supersedes the multiple-handle-per-file behavior in M1.2.**
+- Offer `get_sqlite_connection_status(id)` -> `{id, state}` with states `ready`,
+  `file_missing`, and `unavailable`. `ready` means the file exists and a cheap
+  `PRAGMA schema_version` query succeeded; it **does not** assert database
+  integrity, file identity, or transaction health.
+- If the file goes missing after opening (possible on Unix; usually denied on
+  Windows), preserve the handle in the registry until explicit close.
+- Preserve IPC error normalization and supply a safe Chinese error-message
+  helper for the UI. No filesystem plugin or automatic destructive action.
+- Status checks use `spawn_blocking`, just like the existing M1.2 commands.
+
+## Checks
+
+```sh
+cargo fmt --all
+cargo fmt --all -- --check
+cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --locked -- -D warnings
+cargo test --workspace --locked
+pnpm typecheck
+pnpm test
+node --test scripts/m05-security.test.mjs
+pnpm build
+pnpm tauri build --no-bundle
+```
+
+The tests cover zero-byte files, invalid SQLite headers, duplicate canonical
+paths, close-and-reopen, distinct files, connection capacity, missing-path
+status (Unix), closed/unknown IDs, runtime IPC validation and localized errors.
+
+## Boundaries and limitations
+
+- M1.5 does not implement Explorer UI. If M1.4 is present locally, connect its
+  error presentations and status checks to the new service only after reviewing
+  its actual state-management semantics.
+- No automatic reconnect, retry, integrity scan, `PRAGMA integrity_check`,
+  query execution, file selection, or schema mutation.
+- A replaced database at the same path is not reliably distinguished from the
+  original file; future work may add OS-specific file identity verification.
+- A valid SQLite header alone is not proof that every database page is valid;
+  some damaged databases fail only during later queries.
+- The current global connection-registry mutex serializes status probes and
+  schema reads. Dedicated per-connection workers are left to M2.
+- Tests and GUI observations must be recorded before marking M1.5 accepted.
